{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Task Continuation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Task Continuation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"task continuation task continuation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Task Continuation.md","fileName":"Task Continuation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Task Continuation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[.NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony]]","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Task Continuation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Task Continuation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"task continuation task continuation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Task Continuation.md","fileName":"Task Continuation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Task Continuation","heading":"Task Continuation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A task continuation schedules work that depends on an earlier task's completion. It can inspect the antecedent's result, cancellation, or exception and can be configured to run only under selected completion conditions.\n\nContinuations expose the dependency graph directly, but long chains can become difficult to read and reason about. For naturally asynchronous workflows, C# `async` and `await` usually express the same sequencing with clearer control flow and exception handling.\n\nTask factories also provide continuation forms that begin after all or any task in a group completes. The chosen form should match whether the next step requires the complete result set or can proceed with the first useful completion.","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony","c80